+ *
+ * Machine types (M12; spec/Machine-v5 §1): `dadao-tiny` and `dadao-vast` each
+ * fix their profile at the machine type; there is no runtime `profile=`
+ * selector and no compatibility machine-name alias.
+ * `vast` is Machine-v5-Vast (spec/Machine-v5 §1.1/§6):
+ *   Boot ROM:   0xffff_ffc0_0000 .. 0xffff_ffff_ffff (4 MiB, RO+X)
+ *   reset vec:  0xffff_ffff_0000 (ROM base + 0x3f_0000; last 64 KiB)
+ *   PA RAM:     0 .. 2 GiB (RWX; reached through the PTW identity map)
+ *   hmon SRAM / smon SRAM / cfx_pmem SRAM + full cfx/PTW register file
+ *   `-bios` keeps the 64 KiB reset window; `bootrom-image` takes exactly 4 MiB.
+ * `tiny` is Machine-v5-Tiny (spec/Machine-v5 §1.1/§6):
+ *   Boot ROM:   0xffff_ffff_0000 .. 0xffff_ffff_ffff (64 KiB, RO+X)
+ *   SRAM:       0xffff_ff00_0000 .. 0xffff_ff7f_ffff (8 MiB, RWX)
+ *   reset vec:  0xffff_ffff_0000; raw -kernel at 0xffff_ff01_0000
+ *               (first 0x100 bytes zero, entry 0xffff_ff01_0100);
+ *               ELF PT_LOAD may target the BootROM (crt stub) or the SRAM.
+ *   no cfx register file / PTW / monitor or pmem SRAM / PA-0 alias.
+ *
+ * Loading paths per ADR-0004 D2.2/D2.3 (rev. 2026-10-06, SPEC-107t) and
+ * contract-elf.md §5/§6 -- two paths coexist, selected by the kernel's ELF
+ * magic (0x7f 'E' 'L' 'F'):
+ *
+ *   path A (ELF):   qemu-system-dadao -machine dadao-vast -kernel image.elf
+ *                   before loading, the caller validates the ELF header rules
+ *                   and the PT_LOAD consistency/range rules the upstream
+ *                   loader does not enforce (e_type == ET_EXEC, e_flags
+ *                   version 1 / reserved bits 0, p_filesz <= p_memsz,
+ *                   p_vaddr == p_paddr, segment interval inside the
+ *                   profile's mapped regions; contract-elf.md
+ *                   §1.3/§5.2/§6.1.2).  Vast allows PA RAM only (a boot ROM
+ *                   segment is a load error, user decision D, 2026-10-09);
+ *                   Tiny also allows BootROM segments (crt stub, QEMU-079t).
+ *                   The segment placement (VA=PA, .bss zero-fill) and the
+ *                   entry point (e_entry -> PC) are then delegated to the
+ *                   upstream loader (hw/core/loader.c: load_elf(), the standard
+ *                   API).  No external -bios ROM is used on this path.
+ *
+ *   path B (raw):   qemu-system-dadao -machine dadao-tiny -bios rom.bin -kernel test.bin
+ *                   flat ROM trampoline + flat test binary.  Legacy entry is
+ *                   the RAM base (M1-M3 path); Tiny entry is fixed at
+ *                   kernel_base + kernel_reserved (0x100) and the image's
+ *                   first kernel_reserved bytes must be zero (QEMU-079t).
+ *
+ *   path C (BootROM image, ADR-0043 D1/D2):
+ *                   qemu-system-dadao -machine dadao-vast,bootrom-image=bootrom.bin
+ *                   the image must be exactly the profile ROM size (Vast
+ *                   4 MiB, Tiny 64 KiB) and is loaded at the profile ROM
+ *                   base; the CPU still resets to the profile reset PC.
+ *                   -kernel is optional (an ELF is preloaded into RAM without
+ *                   overriding the reset PC); -bios must not be given.
+ *
+ * Load-stage errors (malformed/oversize images) are reported and cause a
+ * non-zero process exit; they are a different layer from guest faults
+ * (ADR-0004 D4/D5) and never use the exit-port code channel.
+ */
+
